// endpoint_load_feed_through.proto — LoadFeedThrough: bring ONE entry of the
// root feed into the reader's loaded pages, loading every page between. FEED
// section.
//
// WHY ITS OWN RPC. Selecting an expanded-footer item (a detached subagent, a
// shell, a monitor) whose row is older than the reader's oldest loaded page
// cannot be answered by one "older" page: the row may be many pages back, and
// the feed never has holes, so EVERY page from the reader's oldest loaded page
// down to the one holding the row is loaded. The daemon walks those pages
// itself (each one daemon → shim → store, or from daemon memory when it holds
// it) and streams each to the reader as it lands, so the reader paints the
// walk progressively instead of waiting on the whole of it.
//
// The walk is the reader's ordinary `older` walk, advanced: once this stream
// ends, GetFeedPage `next` continues from the oldest page it delivered.

